---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import Email from '../../components/Email.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL, LEGAL_PATHS, withBase } from '../../site';
---
<Legal
  page="deleteAccount"
  lang="en"
  title={`Delete your ${SITE.name} account`}
  shortTitle="Delete account"
  description={`How to delete your ${SITE.name} account, by ${LEGAL.ownerName}, and what data is erased.`}
>
  <Callout icon="cellphone-lock">
    <p>
      If you use the app as a guest, you have no account and we store nothing on our servers. To erase your data, uninstall
      the app.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="how">How to delete your account</h2>
  {LEGAL.inAppDeletion && (
    <>
      <h3>From the app</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Open {SITE.name} and go to <strong>Profile</strong>.</li>
        <li>Under <strong>Account</strong>, tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
        <li>Review what will happen to your groups and choose whether to erase this phone's data too.</li>
        <li>Slide to confirm. The account is deleted right away.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>If you no longer have the app</h3>
    </>
  )}
  <ol>
    <li>Email us at <Email lang="en" subject={`Delete my ${SITE.name} account`} /> with the subject <strong>“Delete my {SITE.name} account”</strong>.</li>
    <li>Send it from the email of the Google or Apple account you use to sign in to the app, so we can confirm the account is yours.</li>
    <li>We delete the account within {LEGAL.deletionDays} business days and let you know when it's done.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="deleted">What is deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account, name, email, profile photo and the link to your Google or Apple account.</li>
    <li>Your name and photo in every shared group and recurring expense: you appear there as “Former user”.</li>
    <li>Any invite codes you created.</li>
    <li>The push notification tokens of your devices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="kept">What is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Expenses and payments you entered in shared groups:</strong> they stay so the other members' numbers still add
      up, without your name or photo and with no link to your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Groups you administered:</strong> they carry on for the other members, and any of them can take over as admin.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Shared recurring expenses you created:</strong> they end and are archived for their members, who can look at
      them but not keep using them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What is on your phone:</strong> it was never on our servers. It stays, unless you choose to erase it too when
      deleting your account, or uninstall the app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server backups:</strong> your data may remain in them for up to {LEGAL.serverBackupDays} days, until they roll
      over. They are only used to restore the service after a failure.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="partial">Delete notification data without deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to delete, together, the notification history received by your account, your alert preferences and
    your devices' push registrations on our servers. Your account, transactions, groups and debts are kept.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Email <Email lang="en" subject={`Delete ${SITE.name} notification data`} /> with the subject <strong>“Delete {SITE.name} notification data”</strong>.</li>
    <li>Include the email you use to sign in. We verify that the account is yours before executing the request; we do not ask for your password.</li>
    <li>We handle the request within {LEGAL.deletionDays} business days after verification and confirm the server deletion.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Notifications stay suspended so opening the app does not recreate those records. You can explicitly reactivate them
    in notification settings to receive new activity; deleted data will not return. Each phone's copy is cleared when a
    compatible app version reconnects. We may ask you to update the app; a phone that stays offline keeps its copy until then.
  </p>
  <p>
    We keep a minimal technical marker and request receipt while the account exists to prevent an old sync from restoring
    the data. They contain no messages or push tokens. Notifications already delivered to the phone's operating system
    or in transit cannot be recalled remotely. Backups roll over within {LEGAL.serverBackupDays} days.
    This request does not erase reports already sent to analytics or crash-report providers.
  </p>
  <h3>Other changes in the app</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Delete an expense you entered:</strong> open it in the group and delete it. This is a separate process and may change shared balances.</li>
    <li><strong>Leave a group or recurring expense:</strong> history and debts remain; leaving does not erase them.</li>
    <li><strong>Sign out:</strong> stops syncing on that phone without deleting the account or shared server data.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>More in the <a href={withBase(LEGAL_PATHS.privacy.en)}>Privacy policy</a>.</p>
</Legal>
